Package: gideon
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Gideon POC <achhetri@webmd.net>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libstdc++6, libgomp1, libportaudio2, libsndfile1
Recommends: pipewire, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber
Description: Gideon - always-on offline voice assistant
 Gideon listens for the phrase "hey gideon" and answers out loud. Speech
 recognition, wake-phrase matching and speech synthesis all run locally on the
 CPU; nothing is sent to any network service and no API key is required.
 .
 This package is self-contained: it vendors its own Python runtime, all Python
 dependencies, and the speech models. It therefore installs and runs identically
 on Ubuntu 24.04 and later regardless of the system Python version, and works
 with no network connection after installation.
 .
 Version 0.1 is a proof of concept: it responds to greetings only and has no
 tool or command execution.
